**Proposition 5.4 (literal polarity is not acquired).** There are
distinct literal laws on every design of Section 1 with identical
entire future service, identical numerical Time/Boundary and identical
acquired predictor class. Thus no inverse from those numbers to
Literal Space exists.

Proof. There is a branch in $K$, since $b\ge3$. Flip only it and
transform the field by the same sign. The law changes along its
nonzero incident edges, while Theorem 3.1 preserves the full service
and every startup record. Theorem 2.3 also counts the $2^{b-1}$
distinct residual laws after full calibration. Their literal polarity
is genuinely different even when every field is zero. No coordinate
choice in Memory selects which physical law occurred. $\square$

